@startbpmn BP14_RollTheDayOver
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP14_RollTheDayOver.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP14_RollTheDayOver.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - the day rolls at local midnight and that is not configurable: BR-44
'   - rollover advances which day is current and nothing else: BR-44
'   - everything that follows from the day focus follows it, Chores included: BR-41, BR-50, BR-107
'   - the previous day's focus and log become history, reachable from the period views: BR-44
'   - rollover creates nothing: no task is spawned, only selecting a routine does that: BR-42, BR-44
'   - rollover archives nothing and closes nothing: BR-44, BR-45
'   - a day never checked out stays checkable out: BR-45
'   - where the new day's focus is empty, its day focus editor is offered: BR-40, BR-44
'   - the offer never interrupts what the user is doing, a drag included: BR-44, BR-66
'   - ignoring the offer leaves the day unfocused: BR-44
'
' Scope: this process advances the date. Setting the new day's focus is BP08, which the offer hands
' over to; reading the previous day as history is BP09; settling it is BP13, and an unchecked day
' stays checkable out afterwards.
'
' Cut: Intent section 5 records this as a process of its own and flags that it may read better as a
' start event inside BP08 - the Software Architect's call. Drawn standalone, which is the cut as it
' stands. Section 5 also says "no user lane": the drawing has one, because BR-44's offer is made to
' the user and ignoring it is a legitimate answer that nothing else can represent.
'
' Call-site collapsing: advancing the date and offering the empty day's editor are one request.
' The offer is what the one write reports, not a second chain.

scheduler pool "Clock" {
  timerStart "Local midnight"
  :Reach the next date;
  send "Roll the day over" to rollIn
  end "Date advanced"
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Rollover due" as rollIn
  call "BP14.01_RollTheDayOver" "Roll the day over" {
    :Advance which date is current;
    rule BR-44
    :Put the new date's focus in play, empty until it is set;
    rule BR-41
    :Carry the previous date's focus and log into history;
    rule BR-45
    :Report whether the new date's focus is empty;
    rule BR-40
  }
  send "The day rolled over" to rolled
  note "Rollover creates nothing and destroys nothing: no task is spawned, nothing is archived and nothing is closed. A date never checked out stays checkable out. Chores follows the new date on its own while it carries work that is not done."
  end "Rollover answered"
}

pool "User" {
  start "At work in Bearing"
  task "Work on whatever is open" as working
  receive "The day rolled over" as rolled
  note "The board in front of the user stays open and a gesture already under way, a drag included, is unaffected."

  if "Is the new date's focus empty?" rule BR-44 then "yes"
    :Read the offer to set the day's focus;
    if "Take the offer?" rule BR-44 then "take it"
      :Open the day focus editor;
      note "Setting the focus is its own process. The offer only opens it."
    else "ignore it"
      :Carry on with what was open;
      note "The offer changes nothing by itself. Ignoring it leaves the day unfocused."
      goto working
    endif
  else "no"
    :Carry on with the new date in play;
  endif

  end "New day in play"
}

@endbpmn
